# Base image vulnerabilities — cannot fix without upstream python:3.11-slim update.
#
# Sunset policy: every ignore carries a "Re-evaluate" date. When the date
# lands, the entry must be removed and either (a) the upstream patch is
# consumed, (b) the CVE is verifiably not exploitable in our container,
# or (c) a new re-eval date is set with a fresh justification. Accumulating
# forever-ignores is forbidden by this policy.

# ncurses buffer overflow — base image dependency, no user-facing exposure.
# Re-evaluate: 2026-06-01 (next Debian 13 point release window).
CVE-2025-69720

# systemd arbitrary code execution — libsystemd0/libudev1 in the base image;
# we run with no systemd instance so RegisterMachine et al. are unreachable.
# Re-evaluate: 2026-06-01.
CVE-2026-29111

# OpenSSL DoS in Debian 13 — pending 3.5.5-1 patch from Debian security.
# Re-evaluate: 2026-05-15 (Debian typically ships within 4-6 weeks of advisory).
CVE-2026-28390

# libcap TOCTOU privilege escalation in cap_set_file (race condition) — the
# container is single-user, no other process calls cap_set_file, race not
# reachable. No upstream fix yet.
# Re-evaluate: 2026-06-30.
CVE-2026-4878

# GnuTLS DTLS zero-length fragment DoS — we use TLS only via httpx /
# AsyncHTTPClient, never DTLS. No code path reaches the affected handler.
# No upstream fix yet in Debian 13.
# Re-evaluate: 2026-06-30.
CVE-2026-33845

# GnuTLS DTLS heap buffer overflow during handshake — same DTLS surface
# as CVE-2026-33845 above. We don't initiate or accept DTLS connections.
# No upstream fix yet in Debian 13.
# Re-evaluate: 2026-06-30.
CVE-2026-33846

# GnuTLS nameConstraints case-sensitive comparison policy bypass — affects
# certificate-validation paths that enforce X.509 nameConstraints. We use
# httpx's default verify path against well-known CAs (no custom name-
# constraint policies). No upstream fix yet in Debian 13.
# Re-evaluate: 2026-06-30.
CVE-2026-3833

# libssh2 vulnerability up to 1.11.1 — libssh2 is pulled in transitively
# by the base image but we never invoke SSH from inside the container
# (no paramiko, no asyncssh, no system ssh client used by application
# code). No upstream fix yet.
# Re-evaluate: 2026-06-30.
CVE-2026-7598

# GnuTLS authentication bypass via NUL character in cert names — we
# don't perform certificate subject-name matching against attacker-
# controlled input. No upstream fix yet.
# Re-evaluate: 2026-06-30.
CVE-2026-42010

# GnuTLS security bypass via incorrect name handling — same attack
# surface as CVE-2026-42010; we don't process attacker-controlled
# cert names anywhere in the codebase. No upstream fix yet.
# Re-evaluate: 2026-06-30.
CVE-2026-42011

# curl/libcurl: wrong file transfer due to incorrect SMB connection
# reuse. We never speak SMB from inside the container (no curl
# invocations from application code use smb:// URLs; httpx is HTTP/HTTPS
# only). Debian 13 base image; no fixed version published as of
# 2026-05-16. Re-evaluate: 2026-06-30.
CVE-2026-5773

# curl/libcurl: information disclosure via cookie leak when reusing
# connections. Httpx (our HTTP client) does not share connection pools
# across hosts and never reuses cookies from a different origin. Debian
# 13 base image; no fixed version published as of 2026-05-16.
# Re-evaluate: 2026-06-30.
CVE-2026-6276

# OpenSSL heap use-after-free in PKCS7_verify(). Application code never
# verifies PKCS7/S-MIME signatures — openssl is only exercised for TLS
# via httpx. Debian 13 base image (libssl3t64/openssl/
# openssl-provider-legacy); no fixed version published as of 2026-06-10.
# Re-evaluate: 2026-06-30.
CVE-2026-45447

# Perl IO::Uncompress::Unzip CPU exhaustion on crafted zip. perl-base
# ships with the Debian 13 base image only as an OS dependency; nothing
# in the container runs perl, let alone on untrusted archives. No fixed
# version published as of 2026-06-10. Re-evaluate: 2026-06-30.
CVE-2026-48959

# SQLite memory corruption / heap-based buffer overflow (SQLite before
# 3.53.2). libsqlite3-0 ships with the Debian 13 base image; exploitation
# requires parsing an attacker-controlled SQLite database or crafted SQL.
# The container never opens untrusted .sqlite files — Chroma/Neo4j/Redis
# are the datastores; sqlite3 is only a transitive OS/stdlib dependency.
# No fixed version (3.53.2) published for Debian 13 as of 2026-06-21.
# Re-evaluate: 2026-07-31.
CVE-2026-11822
CVE-2026-11824
